MiniOS packages the xfwm4-gl fork for Debian Trixie (amd64 and i386).
Upstream version authority: configure.ac, XDT_VERSION_INIT([4.20.0], [-gl1]).
Pinned source: 00710be0c46ec654cd35c1aaec87578b5929d713 (2026-10-01).
The Debian upstream version encodes that base, fork suffix and source commit;
the final -1 is the first packaging revision, not a first-party release.

Create the orig tarball from the pinned upstream Git tree, without debian/:
  git archive --format=tar --prefix=xfwm4-gl-4.20.0+gl1+git20261001.00710be/ \
    00710be0c46ec654cd35c1aaec87578b5929d713 | xz > \
    /path/to/artifacts/xfwm4-gl_4.20.0+gl1+git20261001.00710be.orig.tar.xz
Copy the current source, excluding .git, to a build directory beside that
tarball and use dpkg-source -b there. Build as an unprivileged user.

The package installs the original xfwm4 filenames and cannot coexist with
xfwm4. Session startup and xfconf use their existing names. Runtime renderer
selection and fallback remain upstream defaults; inspect them with:
  xprop -root _XFWM4_RENDER_BACKEND _XFWM4_VSYNC

Validation:
  debian/tests/x11-smoke is an autopkgtest for the installed package. It
  creates a private profile and checks software fallback, EWMH client
  management, resize/fullscreen, and compositor/GL setting toggles.
  Upstream currently has no unit test suite; make check alone is not runtime
  evidence. Run the installed-package test explicitly on both architectures.

  debian/tests/minios.testo exercises a MiniOS Standard amd64 session with
  QXL and the new compositor controls. Use the MiniOS Testo fork with a unique
  prefix. Supply ISO (an exact workspace ISO), PAYLOAD (a QCOW2 disk with an
  ext4 filesystem labelled XFWM4TEST), and SCREENSHOT via --param NAME VALUE.
  The payload contains the clean-built xfwm4-gl amd64 package, live-smoke,
  and any runtime dependencies missing from the selected ISO. The current
  Standard image needs Debian Trixie's libxpresent1_1.0.1-1+b2_amd64.deb.
  A locally installed candidate is package acceptance, not published APT
  repository or rebuilt-ISO acceptance. QXL/Xvfb cover XRender fallback, not
  accelerated OpenGL on physical GPUs.
